 "rulings": [
  {
   "id": "D1",
   "subject": "divergence",
   "as_received": "D1 is accepted as an explicit, stricter full-gzip-read refusal. Document that on D1 inputs the public code changes from E_ARCHIVE_IDENTITY to E_ADAPTER_INPUT. The >=4 GiB CRC bug must not hide under D1.",
   "bounds": [
    "D1 covers a container on which a full read by CPython's gzip module fails, and nothing else. On such an input the port answers \"unreadable archive or manifest\", code E_ADAPTER_INPUT.",
    "The public code can change: where the oracle refuses the content with E_ARCHIVE_IDENTITY, the port refuses the container with E_ADAPTER_INPUT (entry gzip.crc-trailer.identity-mismatch). Where the oracle refuses with E_ADAPTER_INPUT for the content, the message changes and the code does not (entries gzip.crc-trailer.no-manifest, .manifest-not-mapping).",
    "A container CPython's gzip module reads to its end is not a D1 input at any size. test/differential/port_large.py holds that at 4.1 GiB of decompressed data; before the fix round such an archive was refused because of a length truncation in the runtime's crc32."
   ],
   "evidence": [
    "test/vectors/port-divergences.golden (entries gzip.*)",
    "test/vectors/port-large.golden",
    "test/differential/port_primitives.py (kind targz)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "D2",
   "subject": "divergence",
   "as_received": "NaN in `required_names`: name it D2 and fix the comment at config.ts:111-118.",
   "bounds": [
    "D2 covers `required_names` on a set of two or more members that are all numbers and include a NaN. The oracle returns a list whose order follows the address of the NaN object; the port raises TypeError.",
    "No engine module calls `required_names` at the a49b5dc freeze. Were its result handed to `read_lock`, the oracle refuses there, since a NaN is never among the declared names."
   ],
   "evidence": [
    "test/vectors/port-divergences.golden (entries required-names.*)",
    "src/config.ts (comment on `sorted`)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1",
   "subject": "mutants",
   "as_received": "The 8 non-kills are accepted only under a separate classification: 5 redundant survivors, 2 compiler, 1 crash-only. Do not count them as kills (262 stays 262). The e2e witness for archive.L140.4 moves to cook/deploy.",
   "classification": {
    "redundant survivor": [
     "lock.repository.text",
     "lock.repository.password",
